# Example Mosquitto ACL — copy/generate into deploy/mqtt/acl/ (directory) or kit path.
# Legacy (mode OFF):
# user edge:local:fieldbus-1
# topic write openfdd/v1/sites/local/edges/fieldbus-1/#
# topic read openfdd/v1/sites/local/edges/fieldbus-1/commands/#
#
# Wave L tenant namespace (mode ON) — TopicBuilder::with_tenant:
# user edge:acme:bldg2:fieldbus-1
# topic write openfdd/v1/tenants/acme/buildings/bldg2/edges/fieldbus-1/#
# topic read openfdd/v1/tenants/acme/buildings/bldg2/edges/fieldbus-1/commands/#
#
# Kali O2c / P2c MQTT ACL matrix (staging proof — Mint does not ActiveScan OT):
# - Edge A: write telemetry/status/acks for tenant A building only; read commands A only.
# - Deny: tenant B topics, openfdd/v1/tenants/+/… wildcards, cross-tenant #.
# - Central: read tenant trees it serves; write commands only to owned edges.
# - Mount generated ACL at mosquitto acl_file; never ship long-lived edge keys in repo.
